# Quests and questlines (DESIGN.md §17.1, Q1): `quests <dir>` reads and checks a directory's
# without loading it; once a world loads, `quests` lists its own (Q5).

# Every quest, whose it is and where it sits, then each questline's steps. A quest in a
# questline is the questline's giver's unless it names its own, as the captain's dog does.
quests docs/examples/riverhold
quests docs/examples/riverhold lost_dog

# One quest: its gate, then each stage with its requirements and choices.
quests docs/examples/riverhold watch_oath
assert quests docs/examples/riverhold watch_oth == error: unknown quest 'watch_oth' (did you mean 'watch_oath'?)

# Quests are checked with everything else, and a world whose quests reconcile loads with them.
assert validate docs/examples/riverhold == docs/examples/riverhold loads: 6 characters, 5 factions, 6 actions, 7 relations, 6 outcomes, 10 quests and 1 questline
assert quests == error: no world is loaded yet: use load <dir> first
load content/sample
quests

# Warnings follow the list: closing leftovers on a step that needs every quest does nothing.
quests crates/cli/tests/fixtures/worlds/odd_jobs
assert quests crates/cli/tests/fixtures/worlds/diamonds == no quests in crates/cli/tests/fixtures/worlds/diamonds
